# TaskFlow Project Structure

This document outlines the directory structure and important files in the TaskFlow project - a full-stack task management application.

## Project Overview
TaskFlow is a multi-tier application consisting of:
- **Backend**: .NET 9 Minimal API with Entity Framework Core
- **Frontend**: Next.js 15 with TypeScript and Tailwind CSS
- **Functions**: Azure Functions for background processing
- **Database**: SQL Server with local Azurite emulation

## Root Directory Structure

```
my-taskflow/
├── .cursor/rules/              # Cursor AI rules and guidelines
├── backend/                    # .NET API backend
├── frontend/                   # Next.js React frontend  
├── functions/                  # Azure Functions
├── docs/                       # Project documentation
├── __blobstorage__/           # Azurite blob storage (local dev)
├── __queuestorage__/          # Azurite queue storage (local dev)
└── *.json                     # Azurite database files (local dev)
```

